latform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on CentOS Stream 10 with kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64. Node1 used the CentOS repository's Postfix 3.8.5 package, which was active after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-64568aa4672240ff","cmd-0a7b5e71a1c04130","cmd-1fdadf9851c44aa9","cmd-60875c412e0b4d01","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"The implementation was focused and ended with healthy package state, no failed services, and only the required SMTP listener added. One unnecessary test mutation occurred: cmd-4d869d2490bd4962 submitted to nobody@branch.test, which was actually a valid system account and delivered into root's mailbox; no cleanup was shown, so that message appears retained. The mandatory restart commands also left small /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log files on both nodes; their creation supported the restart protocol, but the retained files are avoidable residue. The initial Postfix startup failure was diagnosed and corrected, so it is not treated as an unnecessary mutation or final defect.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4d869d2490bd4962","cmd-eaaa4679c5614057","cmd-12fd8f8c1ce74468","cmd-3db30dc7b76f4ec8","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct end-to-end SMTP evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently on both nodes: each had a healthy pre-restart observation and acknowledgement, a changed post-restart boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered connectivity and delivery behavior. Hygiene is reduced only by one misdirected test message and two retained reboot log files.","limitations":["The handover files were directly rehashed after execution only on node1. Preservation on node2 is supported by its preparation baseline and the absence of any executor command targeting that directory, rather than by a final node2 hash observation.","The retained root-mailbox test message was not explicitly inspected in the final snapshot, although direct delivery was recorded and no removal command appears later in the timeline."]}
